  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "${\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({i}^{2}+{j}^{2})=$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we write out the inner summation by summing over the index $j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({i}^{2}+{j}^{2}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}[{\\sum }_{j=1}^{2}({i}^{2}+{j}^{2})] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}[({i}^{2}+{1}^{2})+({i}^{2}+{2}^{2})] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(2{i}^{2}+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we sum over the index $i:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{2}(2{i}^{2}+5) & =[2(1)^{2}+5]+[2(2)^{2}+5] \\\\  & =7+13 \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$",
